Subject: [PATCH] server: do not run the chat parser on the non-OAI /completion path

Applies to ggml-org/llama.cpp b10569 (commit 5a32f7b, 2026-08-21).
Apply with:  git -C ~/opt/llama.cpp/src apply <this file>

WHAT GOES WRONG

`/completion` serializes through `server_task_result_cmpl_final::to_json_non_oaicompat()`,
which references `oaicompat_msg` exactly zero times. But `update()` populates it
unconditionally, and populating it means running `common_chat_parse` ->
`common_chat_peg_parse`, which *throws* on output it cannot parse
(common/chat.cpp:3873). The exception escapes as an HTTP 500 and the completion is
lost. The parse is dead work on that path, and it is dead work that can fail.

Any request that forces its own output length can reach it. With `n_predict` +
`ignore_eos` the generation stops wherever the budget runs out, which can be
mid-UTF-8-character, and the parser rejects a lone continuation byte:

    common_chat_peg_parse: unparsed Content-only output: <0xB2>
    srv operator(): got exception: {"error":{"code":500,"message":"The model
      produced output that does not match the expected Content-only format"}}

Measured at 2 failures per 200 requests on Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct Q4_K_M with
random-token prompts, and deterministic for a given (prompt, n_predict).

WHY THE EXISTING LENIENT HANDLING DOES NOT COVER IT

chat.cpp:3840 already sets COMMON_PEG_PARSE_FLAG_LENIENT, and there is a recovery
path for unparseable output -- but it is gated `if (is_partial && result.end > 0)`
(chat.cpp:3851). A non-streaming final result has `is_partial == false`, so it never
applies; and when the bad byte lands at position 0, `result.end == 0`, so the
streaming path throws too. That is why `"stream": true` returns the same error as
its first SSE event rather than avoiding it.

This is the same failure as ggml-org/llama.cpp#20193, reached through `max_tokens`
instead. PR #20191 (merged 2026-03-08) added the lenient flag and the partial
recovery above; both are already present in b10569 and neither covers the final
result. The call is still unconditional on master.

WHAT THIS CHANGES

Guarding on `res_type` restores the invariant that a response format which does not
use the parsed message does not pay for it -- and cannot fail because of it. The
OpenAI, Anthropic and Responses paths are untouched, and `timings` is unaffected:
verified `f18_status == "full"` with prefill/decode still reported after the patch.

diff --git a/tools/server/server-task.cpp b/tools/server/server-task.cpp
index 258cdcf..66d73ca 100644
--- a/tools/server/server-task.cpp
+++ b/tools/server/server-task.cpp
@@ -992,7 +992,11 @@ void server_task_result_cmpl_partial::update(task_result_state & state) {
     if (is_begin) {
         return; // begin marker only flushes headers, skip parsing
     }
-    state.update_chat_msg(content, true, oaicompat_msg_diffs);
+    if (res_type != TASK_RESPONSE_TYPE_NONE) {
+        // Same reasoning as the final result: the streaming /completion path renders
+        // through to_json_non_oaicompat() and never reads the parsed message.
+        state.update_chat_msg(content, true, oaicompat_msg_diffs);
+    }
 
     // Copy current state for use in to_json_*() (reflects state BEFORE this chunk)
     thinking_block_started = state.thinking_block_started;
diff --git a/tools/server/server-task.h b/tools/server/server-task.h
index 25ff015..c481a07 100644
--- a/tools/server/server-task.h
+++ b/tools/server/server-task.h
@@ -365,7 +365,11 @@ struct server_task_result_cmpl_final : server_task_result {
 
     virtual void update(task_result_state & state) override {
         is_updated = true;
-        oaicompat_msg = state.update_chat_msg(content, false, oaicompat_msg_diffs);
+        if (res_type != TASK_RESPONSE_TYPE_NONE) {
+            // /completion renders through to_json_non_oaicompat(), which never reads
+            // oaicompat_msg. Parsing there buys nothing and can throw.
+            oaicompat_msg = state.update_chat_msg(content, false, oaicompat_msg_diffs);
+        }
 
         oai_resp_id = state.oai_resp_id;
         oai_resp_reasoning_id = state.oai_resp_reasoning_id;
